{0 awskit-s3-lwt}

Generic Lwt adapter for Awskit S3.

The public entrypoint is {!module:Awskit_s3_lwt}. This package connects the
runtime-neutral {!module:Awskit_s3} operation surface to a caller-supplied
Awskit Lwt runtime.

Use it when an application needs a custom Lwt HTTP backend. Use the
[awskit-s3-lwt-unix] package when the ready Lwt + Unix S3 client is enough.

{1 Runtime Shape}

Use {!module:Awskit_s3_lwt.Make} with a [Cohttp_lwt.S.Client] implementation
when the application owns the Lwt HTTP backend, context, credentials, region,
clock, retry sleep, and timeout policy.

This package exposes the S3 operation modules, in-memory body helpers, and
[Body.of_lwt_stream] for custom streaming uploads. It intentionally does not
own Unix local-path helpers or managed file transfer helpers; those live in
[awskit-s3-lwt-unix].

Custom stream bodies must declare the exact [content_length]. Mark them
replayable only when retrying can recreate the same bytes from the beginning.
Response readers are scoped to the [Object.get] consumer callback.
